{"black_box_warning":{"current_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current DailyMed label.","fda_source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf"],"proposed_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in FDA Acthar Gel prescribing information.","rationale":"The no-boxed-warning conclusion is supported by the FDA accessdata label for Acthar Gel, which contains warnings and precautions but no boxed-warning section or boxed-warning text. The current row wording and source rely on DailyMed, which is not permissible for this field.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect"},"blocking_questions":[],"fact_checks":[{"current_value":"Infectious: infection 20%, neurologic: convulsion 12%, vascular/cardiac: hypertension 11%, behavioral: irritability 7%, constitutional: pyrexia 5%, cardiac: cardiac hypertrophy 3%, endocrine: Cushingoid 3%, GI: diarrhea 3%, GI: vomiting 3%, GI: decreased appetite 3% (FDA infantile-spasms data at recommended 75 U/m2 BID dose).","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"Infectious: infection 20%, neurologic: convulsion 12%, vascular/cardiac: hypertension 11%, behavioral: irritability 7%, constitutional: pyrexia 5%, cardiac: cardiac hypertrophy 3%, endocrine: Cushingoid 3%, GI: diarrhea 3%, GI: vomiting 3%, GI: decreased appetite 3% (FDA infantile-spasms data at recommended 75 U/m2 BID dose).","rationale":"FDA labeling tabulates these adverse-reaction percentages for infants and children under 2 years treated with Acthar Gel at the recommended 75 U/m2 twice-daily regimen.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"adrenocorticotropic hormone; ACTH; corticotropin","field":"alternate_generic_names","proposed_value":"adrenocorticotropic hormone; ACTH; corticotropin","rationale":"FDA orphan-drug record lists repository corticotropin or adrenocorticotropic hormone, and NCBI MeSH lists ACTH and corticotropin as entry terms for adrenocorticotropic hormone.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/opdlisting/oopd/detailedIndex.cfm?cfgridkey=168103","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sites/entrez?Cmd=DetailsSearch&Db=mesh&Term=%22Adrenocorticotropic+Hormone%22%5BMeSH+Terms%5D"]},{"current_value":"Yes","field":"available_in_us","proposed_value":"Yes","rationale":"Acthar Gel has FDA labeling and an FDA orphan marketing approval record for infantile spasms, supporting US availability.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/opdlisting/oopd/detailedIndex.cfm?cfgridkey=168103"]},{"current_value":"Not a CYP inducer/inhibitor; FDA label notes steroidogenic/electrolyte effects and that Acthar Gel may accentuate electrolyte loss associated with diuretics.","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting","proposed_value":"Formal drug-drug interaction studies have not been performed; FDA label states Acthar Gel may accentuate the electrolyte loss associated with diuretic therapy. No FDA-label CYP induction/inhibition interaction was identified.","rationale":"The FDA label supports the diuretic/electrolyte interaction and states formal drug-drug interaction studies have not been performed. I did not find FDA-label support for the stronger statement that it is not a CYP inducer/inhibitor.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"missing_source","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Epileptic spasms / infantile spasms","field":"epilepsy_type","proposed_value":"Epileptic spasms / infantile spasms","rationale":"FDA labeling indicates Acthar Gel as monotherapy for infantile spasms in infants and children under 2 years of age; FDA orphan record uses the same infantile-spasms indication.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/opdlisting/oopd/detailedIndex.cfm?cfgridkey=168103"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed Acthar Gel label (https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=7b48ddec-e815-45f4-9ca0-5c0daaf56f30); FDA orphan drug designation/approval record for repository corticotropin/adrenocorticotropic hormone (https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/opdlisting/oopd/detailedIndex.cfm?cfgridkey=168103); FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA Acthar Gel label, NDA 008372/S-074, revised 02/2024 (https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf); FDA orphan drug designation/approval record for repository corticotropin/adrenocorticotropic hormone, H.P. Acthar Gel, infantile spasms marketing approval 10/15/2010 (https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/opdlisting/oopd/detailedIndex.cfm?cfgridkey=168103); NCBI MeSH Adrenocorticotropic Hormone entry terms for ACTH/corticotropin aliases (https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sites/entrez?Cmd=DetailsSearch&Db=mesh&Term=%22Adrenocorticotropic+Hormone%22%5BMeSH+Terms%5D); Tran et al. 2022 scoping review, PMID 34902005, for corticotropin RCT context (https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34902005/).","rationale":"The current source field relies on DailyMed and duplicates FDA/DailyMed labeling. Replace with trusted FDA/NCBI/PubMed sources that support the row facts and RCT context.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/opdlisting/oopd/detailedIndex.cfm?cfgridkey=168103","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sites/entrez?Cmd=DetailsSearch&Db=mesh&Term=%22Adrenocorticotropic+Hormone%22%5BMeSH+Terms%5D","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34902005/"]},{"current_value":"Repository corticotropin injectable gel; multi-dose vial for intramuscular use in infantile spasms; prefilled subcutaneous injector for adult non-seizure indications","field":"formulations_available","proposed_value":"Repository corticotropin injectable gel; multi-dose vial for intramuscular use in infantile spasms; prefilled subcutaneous injector for adult non-seizure indications","rationale":"FDA labeling lists the multi-dose vial and 40-unit/80-unit single-dose pre-filled SelfJect injectors; it specifies infantile-spasms dosing must use the vial intramuscularly and that the SelfJect injector is for adults only.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"ACTH plasma half-life about 15 min after IV administration; pharmacokinetics of Acthar Gel not adequately characterized","field":"half_life_range","proposed_value":"ACTH plasma half-life about 15 min after IV administration; pharmacokinetics of Acthar Gel not adequately characterized","rationale":"FDA labeling states ACTH disappears rapidly after IV administration, plasma half-life is about 15 minutes, and Acthar Gel pharmacokinetics have not been adequately characterized.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Limited/unknown; peptide hormone mixture with adrenal cortical target effects rather than a conventional hepatic/renal ASM metabolism profile","field":"major_organ_for_metabolism","proposed_value":"Limited/unknown; FDA label states pharmacokinetics of Acthar Gel have not been adequately characterized and describes Acthar Gel as a naturally sourced complex mixture of adrenocorticotropic hormone analogs and other pituitary peptides with adrenal cortical effects.","rationale":"The label supports limited/unknown pharmacokinetics and adrenal cortical effects. The comparison to a conventional hepatic/renal ASM metabolism profile is an inference not directly sourced in the row.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"missing_source","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Infantile spasms: 150 U/m2/day divided BID during the 2-week treatment course, followed by taper.","field":"maximum_approved_daily_dose","proposed_value":"Infantile spasms: 150 U/m2/day divided BID during the 2-week treatment course, followed by taper.","rationale":"FDA labeling gives 150 U/m2 daily, divided into twice-daily IM injections of 75 U/m2 for 2 weeks, then taper over 2 weeks.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Moderate","field":"mechanism_confidence","proposed_value":"Moderate","rationale":"Moderate confidence is consistent with FDA labeling: the infantile-spasms mechanism is unknown, but adrenal cortical stimulation and melanocortin-receptor binding are described.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA labeling states the mechanism of action in infantile spasms is unknown; Acthar Gel and endogenous ACTH stimulate adrenal cortical secretion of cortisol, corticosterone, aldosterone, and weak androgenic substances, and Acthar Gel is also reported to bind melanocortin receptors.","field":"mechanism_of_action","proposed_value":"FDA labeling states the mechanism of action in infantile spasms is unknown; Acthar Gel and endogenous ACTH stimulate adrenal cortical secretion of cortisol, corticosterone, aldosterone, and weak androgenic substances, and Acthar Gel is also reported to bind melanocortin receptors.","rationale":"This matches FDA label section 12.1.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed Acthar Gel label (https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=7b48ddec-e815-45f4-9ca0-5c0daaf56f30)","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA Acthar Gel label, NDA 008372/S-074, section 12.1 Mechanism of Action (https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf)","rationale":"DailyMed should be replaced with the FDA accessdata label source.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA label","field":"mechanism_source_tier","proposed_value":"FDA label","rationale":"The proposed mechanism source is an FDA accessdata label, so the source tier remains correct.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA-labeled infantile-spasms regimen: 150 U/m2/day divided BID for 2 weeks before taper; supportive trial studied lower-dose regimens but labeled dosing uses 150 U/m2/day.","field":"minimum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"FDA-labeled infantile-spasms regimen: 150 U/m2/day divided BID for 2 weeks before taper; supportive trial studied lower-dose regimens but labeled dosing uses 150 U/m2/day.","rationale":"FDA labeling gives this regimen and describes a supportive high-dose versus low-dose trial outside the placebo-controlled RCT section.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A","field":"pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links","proposed_value":"N/A","rationale":"No qualifying phase II/III placebo-controlled epilepsy RCT link is present. FDA-labeled infantile-spasms evidence consists of an ACTH-vs-prednisone randomized study and a high-dose versus low-dose supportive trial, not a placebo-only controlled epilepsy RCT. A placebo-controlled RCI RCT exists for multiple sclerosis relapse, but that is not an epilepsy/seizure indication.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34902005/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34984839/"]},{"current_value":"ACTH; adrenocorticotropic hormone; corticotropin; Acthar Gel; H.P. Acthar Gel","field":"pubmed_search_aliases","proposed_value":"ACTH; adrenocorticotropic hormone; corticotropin; Acthar Gel; H.P. Acthar Gel","rationale":"Aliases are supported by NCBI MeSH and FDA label/orphan records. They should not be separate drug rows.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sites/entrez?Cmd=DetailsSearch&Db=mesh&Term=%22Adrenocorticotropic+Hormone%22%5BMeSH+Terms%5D","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/opdlisting/oopd/detailedIndex.cfm?cfgridkey=168103"]},{"current_value":"No QT interval effect described in FDA labeling; monitor for hypertension, salt/water retention, hypokalemia, and cardiac hypertrophy in infantile-spasms safety data.","field":"qt_interval_effect","proposed_value":"No QT interval effect described in FDA labeling; monitor for hypertension, salt/water retention, hypokalemia, and cardiac hypertrophy in infantile-spasms safety data.","rationale":"FDA labeling emphasizes blood pressure, salt/water retention, hypokalemia, and cardiac hypertrophy in the safety data; no QT warning was identified in the FDA label reviewed.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Acthar Gel; H.P. Acthar Gel","field":"trade_names","proposed_value":"Acthar Gel; H.P. Acthar Gel","rationale":"FDA labeling uses Acthar Gel and FDA orphan record lists H.P. Acthar Gel.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/opdlisting/oopd/detailedIndex.cfm?cfgridkey=168103"]},{"current_value":"Infantile spasms: 150 U/m2/day divided as 75 U/m2 IM twice daily for 2 weeks, then gradual taper over 2 weeks per FDA label.","field":"typical_doses_per_day","proposed_value":"Infantile spasms: 150 U/m2/day divided as 75 U/m2 IM twice daily for 2 weeks, then gradual taper over 2 weeks per FDA label.","rationale":"FDA labeling gives the same infantile-spasms dosing and taper schedule.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"1952 initial U.S. approval; FDA orphan marketing approval for infantile spasms 10/15/2010.","field":"year_fda_cleared","proposed_value":"1952 initial U.S. approval; FDA orphan marketing approval for infantile spasms 10/15/2010.","rationale":"FDA label states Initial U.S. Approval: 1952; FDA orphan record lists marketing approval for infantile spasms on 10/15/2010.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/opdlisting/oopd/detailedIndex.cfm?cfgridkey=168103"]}],"generic_name":"repository corticotropin","missing_rcts":[],"outcome_checks":[{"current_value":"N/A","field":"diff_50_responder_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"N/A","rationale":"No qualifying placebo-controlled epilepsy RCT with an RR50 endpoint was identified for repository corticotropin/ACTH in infantile spasms. FDA-labeled infantile-spasms trials use active comparator or dose comparison and responder definitions based on spasm cessation plus hypsarrhythmia resolution, not RR50 versus placebo.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"not_applicable","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34902005/"]},{"current_value":"N/A","field":"diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"N/A","rationale":"No qualifying placebo-controlled epilepsy RCT with median percent seizure-change outcome was identified for this row. Retain N/A.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"not_applicable","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34902005/"]},{"current_value":"N/A","field":"diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"N/A","rationale":"No qualifying placebo-controlled epilepsy RCT with placebo-differential seizure freedom was identified. FDA-labeled response data are from ACTH-vs-prednisone and dose-comparison infantile-spasms studies, not placebo-controlled epilepsy studies.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"not_applicable","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34902005/"]}],"overall_status":"needs_update","proposed_row_updates":[{"current_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current DailyMed label.","field":"fda_black_box_warning","proposed_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in FDA Acthar Gel prescribing information.","reason":"Black-box warning verification must use FDA sources, not DailyMed. FDA accessdata label contains no boxed-warning section/text.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Not a CYP inducer/inhibitor; FDA label notes steroidogenic/electrolyte effects and that Acthar Gel may accentuate electrolyte loss associated with diuretics.","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting","proposed_value":"Formal drug-drug interaction studies have not been performed; FDA label states Acthar Gel may accentuate the electrolyte loss associated with diuretic therapy. No FDA-label CYP induction/inhibition interaction was identified.","reason":"The diuretic/electrolyte statement is supported; the stronger CYP statement lacks a named supporting source in the row.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Limited/unknown; peptide hormone mixture with adrenal cortical target effects rather than a conventional hepatic/renal ASM metabolism profile","field":"major_organ_for_metabolism","proposed_value":"Limited/unknown; FDA label states pharmacokinetics of Acthar Gel have not been adequately characterized and describes Acthar Gel as a naturally sourced complex mixture of adrenocorticotropic hormone analogs and other pituitary peptides with adrenal cortical effects.","reason":"Keeps the limited/unknown classification but replaces an unsourced metabolism-profile inference with FDA-label wording.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf"]}],"rct_link_checks":[{"label":"Sun 2023 melatonin supplementation add-on trial","pmid":"37909654","proposed_action":"Do not add to repository corticotropin placebo-controlled RCT links.","rationale":"The trial intervention is melatonin supplementation for infantile epileptic spasms syndrome, not repository corticotropin/ACTH.","status":"wrong_drug","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37909654/"},{"label":"Sun 2022 melatonin supplementation trial protocol","pmid":"35788069","proposed_action":"Do not add to repository corticotropin placebo-controlled RCT links.","rationale":"This is a melatonin protocol, not repository corticotropin/ACTH efficacy evidence.","status":"wrong_drug","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35788069/"},{"label":"Bitton 2012 flunarizine add-on therapy","pmid":"22889307","proposed_action":"Do not add to repository corticotropin placebo-controlled RCT links.","rationale":"Primary intervention is flunarizine add-on therapy in children with infantile spasms, not repository corticotropin/ACTH.","status":"wrong_drug","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22889307/"},{"label":"Murck 1998 magnesium and ACTH secretion during sleep","pmid":"9683002","proposed_action":"Do not add to repository corticotropin placebo-controlled RCT links.","rationale":"Study concerns magnesium effects on endogenous ACTH secretion and sleep physiology in men, not repository corticotropin treatment for seizures.","status":"wrong_drug","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9683002/"},{"label":"Dyken 1985 valproate in infantile spasms","pmid":"3939740","proposed_action":"Do not add to repository corticotropin placebo-controlled RCT links.","rationale":"Trial is about valproate, not repository corticotropin/ACTH as the tested intervention.","status":"wrong_drug","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/3939740/"},{"label":"Hrachovy 1983 ACTH vs prednisone in infantile spasms","pmid":"6312008","proposed_action":"Do not add to placebo-controlled epilepsy RCT links; may be cited only as non-qualifying active-comparator evidence if project scope allows.","rationale":"This is a randomized double-blind comparison of ACTH versus prednisone with placebo/double-dummy elements, but it lacks a placebo-only efficacy control arm and is outside the row's placebo-controlled RCT outcome section.","status":"not_placebo_rct","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6312008/"},{"label":"Small 1977 ACTH 4-10 and ECT-induced memory dysfunction","pmid":"193359","proposed_action":"Do not add to repository corticotropin placebo-controlled RCT links.","rationale":"Study uses an ACTH fragment in an ECT memory context, not repository corticotropin/Acthar for epilepsy or infantile spasms.","status":"wrong_drug","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/193359/"}],"source_updates":[{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed Acthar Gel label (https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=7b48ddec-e815-45f4-9ca0-5c0daaf56f30); FDA orphan drug designation/approval record for repository corticotropin/adrenocorticotropic hormone (https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/opdlisting/oopd/detailedIndex.cfm?cfgridkey=168103); FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA Acthar Gel label, NDA 008372/S-074, revised 02/2024 (https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf); FDA orphan drug designation/approval record for repository corticotropin/adrenocorticotropic hormone, H.P. Acthar Gel, infantile spasms marketing approval 10/15/2010 (https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/opdlisting/oopd/detailedIndex.cfm?cfgridkey=168103); NCBI MeSH Adrenocorticotropic Hormone entry terms for ACTH/corticotropin aliases (https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sites/entrez?Cmd=DetailsSearch&Db=mesh&Term=%22Adrenocorticotropic+Hormone%22%5BMeSH+Terms%5D); Tran et al. 2022 scoping review, PMID 34902005, for corticotropin RCT context (https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34902005/).","reason":"Use trusted FDA/NCBI/PubMed sources and remove DailyMed from the source list.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/opdlisting/oopd/detailedIndex.cfm?cfgridkey=168103","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sites/entrez?Cmd=DetailsSearch&Db=mesh&Term=%22Adrenocorticotropic+Hormone%22%5BMeSH+Terms%5D","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34902005/"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_label; setid=7b48ddec-e815-45f4-9ca0-5c0daaf56f30; published=Dec 08, 2025; title=ACTHAR (REPOSITORY CORTICOTROPIN) INJECTION ACTHAR (REPOSITORY CORTICOTROPIN) INJECTION [MALLINCKRODT ARD LLC]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=7b48ddec-e815-45f4-9ca0-5c0daaf56f30","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA Acthar Gel label, NDA 008372/S-074, revised 02/2024; status=no_boxed_warning_identified_in_fda_label; url=https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf","reason":"DailyMed is not permissible for FDA boxed-warning verification; use FDA accessdata labeling.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed Acthar Gel label (https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=7b48ddec-e815-45f4-9ca0-5c0daaf56f30)","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA Acthar Gel label, NDA 008372/S-074, section 12.1 Mechanism of Action (https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf)","reason":"Replace DailyMed with the FDA accessdata label source.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf"]}],"summary":"Most dose, indication, adverse-event, alias, formulation, mechanism, and approval-date facts are verified against FDA/NCBI sources. The row needs source cleanup because it relies on DailyMed, including for the FDA boxed-warning field, and two wording updates should be considered for unsupported CYP/metabolism claims. No qualifying placebo-controlled epilepsy RCT or placebo-differential seizure outcome was identified, so the RCT/outcome N/A cells are retained."}
